content.text:
Both faults are now clear, so I'll write up the findings.

Two root causes, both pod-level outages rather than network or HTTP faults. Frontend's user-facing errors come from search and profile, and nothing else in the path has a fault of its own.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(value) AS min_restarts, max(value) AS max_restarts, count(*) AS samples FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "search pod restarts rose to 6-8 in the abnormal window, up from a constant 3 in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.ready' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search pod reports container not ready (0) for every sample in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name = 'search' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search deployment has zero available replicas throughout the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, avg(duration)/1e6 AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "frontend's search calls fail fast with Error status (about 0.01 ms), with no search server spans after startup."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "profile",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(value) AS min_restarts, max(value) AS max_restarts, count(*) AS samples FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'profile%' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "profile pod restarts rose to 6-8 in the abnormal window, up from a constant 3 in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.ready' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'profile%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "profile pod is never ready (0) in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name = 'profile' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "profile deployment has zero available replicas throughout the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, avg(duration)/1e6 AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'profile%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "frontend's profile calls fail fast with Error status (about 0.01 ms); profile emits no spans after startup."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND level = 'ERROR' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "frontend logs 'Search service failed' errors (754 of 1197) once search is unavailable."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "profile",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND level = 'ERROR' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "frontend logs 'Get profiles failed' errors (443 of 1197) once profile is unavailable."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

